# CODEOWNERS - adopter-customisable stub (every rule below is intentionally commented out).
#
# GitHub uses this file to request reviews automatically from the owners of the
# matched paths. Ownership rules are last-match-wins: the final matching pattern
# in the file is the one that applies.
#
# Why an empty stub ships with the template:
# .github/rulesets/protect-main-branch.json sets "require_code_owner_review": false.
# That setting is only meaningful once a CODEOWNERS file exists, so this stub makes the
# ruleset option a real, flippable switch rather than a reference to a missing file.
#
# To turn it on:
#   1. Uncomment and edit the rules below (owners must have write access to the repository).
#   2. Set "require_code_owner_review": true in .github/rulesets/protect-main-branch.json.
#   3. Re-apply the ruleset: python3 scripts/setup_branch_protection.py
#      (see docs/BRANCH_PROTECTION.md).
#
# Note: with a single-maintainer repository, requiring code owner review can block your
# own pull requests, because GitHub will not accept a review from the PR author.
#
# Default owner for everything in the repository:
# * @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
#
# Agent rules of engagement and skill definitions:
# /AGENTS.md              @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
# /.agents/skills/        @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
#
# CI, governance and repository rulesets:
# /.github/               @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
#
# Template automation scripts and their tests:
# /scripts/               @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
# /tests/                 @<GITHUB_OWNER_PLACEHOLDER>
